  "text": "**Solution 1 (22) is wrong.** Since $K_4 \\subseteq K_5 - e$, any coloring with no red $K_5$ and no blue $K_4$ also has no blue $K_5 - e$. So $R(K_5, K_5-e) \\ge R(K_5, K_4) = 25$, which rules out 22. Its quoted values are also suspect: $R(K_4, K_4-e) = 10$, not 11.\n\n**Solution 2 (30) is unsupported.** Its opening bounds are sound: $R(K_5, K_4) = 25$ gives the lower bound and $R(5,5)$ the upper bound. But the claimed construction on $K_{29}$ and the upper-bound argument are asserted, not shown. The \"$26.5$\" recursive bound is not a valid derivation, and the table is not checked against any source. I cannot confirm that 30 is the exact value.\n\n**Solution 3 (34) is unsupported.** Its bounds $25 \\le R \\le 48$ are valid, but the \"refined analysis\" uses $R(K_4, K_5-e) = 22$, which I don't believe is the known value (I recall it being larger, around 28). The claim that a computer-assisted verification established 34 is not backed by any citation or argument. I cannot confirm 34.\n\nI could not verify the exact value from memory with confidence, and none of the three solutions gives a checkable justification for its answer. The only firmly refuted answer is 22. I have no way to look up Radziszowski's survey here, so I am not confident that any of 22, 30, or 34 is the correct exact value.\n\nCHOICE: NONE",
